{"reviewer_participant_id": "actor:founder-c-reviewer-fable-03", "reviews": [{"case_id": "case:8c347d0471b4ab2fcc31", "verdict": "demonstrated_issue", "bounded_statement": "In this case the emission-weighted comparison was computed against the complement (1 - marker) of the supplied panel column rather than against the panel values in the coding supplied: only 7 of 24 units match the complemented panel, yielding the reported emission 11.2500 and rate 0.291667 (7/24), whereas the supplied-coding comparison gives 17 matches, emission 18.7500 and rate 0.708333. The report's selected result therefore presents a rate and emission derived from the complemented panel while simultaneously claiming (and correctly stating the count for) the supplied-coding agreement of 17/24, an internal contradiction since 17/24 ≠ 0.291667.", "root_cause": "workflow/analysis.py defines panel_indicator(marker_value) = 1 - marker_value and builds panel_values from it before computing the concordance weights, so every emission weight and the derived agreement rate use the complemented panel column; the agreement count of 17 shown in the report is only recovered afterwards by subtracting the complement-based match count from the unit total (agreement_count = unit_count - matched_count), masking the substitution while the rate (Fraction(matched_count, unit_count) = 7/24) and emission total (11.25) remain complement-based.", "issue_class": "issue-class:complemented-panel-for-supplied-panel-emission", "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The workflow complements the supplied panel marker before any comparison.", "observed_value": "panel_indicator returns 1 - marker_value and feeds panel_values", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 20, "end_line": 21, "quoted_text": "def panel_indicator(marker_value):\n    return 1 - marker_value"}, {"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 37, "end_line": 38, "quoted_text": "panel_values = [panel_indicator(marker_value) for marker_value in panel_markers]\nweight_values = [concordance_weight(observed_calls[position], panel_values[position]) for position in range(unit_count)]"}]}, {"description": "The reported rate and emission come from the complemented comparison while the count is arithmetically inverted to look like the supplied-coding count.", "observed_value": "agreement_count = 24 - 7 = 17 but agreement_rate = 7/24", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 53, "end_line": 55, "quoted_text": "matched_count = matched_fraction.numerator\nagreement_count = unit_count - matched_count\nagreement_rate = Fraction(matched_count, unit_count)"}]}, {"description": "The report's selected result pairs an agreement count of 17/24 with a rate of 0.291667 and emission 11.2500; 17/24 = 0.708333, and 11.25 = 7\u00d71 + 17\u00d70.25 is only obtainable from the complemented-panel comparison (7 matches), not from the supplied coding (17 matches, which would give 18.75).", "observed_value": "17 of 24 units, rate 0.291667, emission 11.2500", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 16, "end_line": 18, "quoted_text": "Units whose observed call equals the supplied panel value: 17\nPer-unit agreement rate used by the emission accumulation: 0.291667\nAccumulated emission value (sum of the per-unit concordance weights): 11.2500"}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 20, "end_line": 20, "quoted_text": "[selected-result] Observed-versus-panel agreement is 17 of 24 units, per-unit agreement rate 0.291667, accumulated emission value 11.2500."}]}, {"description": "Independent recount from the staged data: rows ISO-004, ISO-007, ISO-011, ISO-015, ISO-018, ISO-021, ISO-023 are the only 7 rows where observed_resistance_call differs from panel_gyra_marker as supplied, so supplied-coding agreement is 17/24 and complement agreement is 7/24; the reported rate matches the complement figure.", "observed_value": "7 discordant rows under supplied coding", "source_spans": [{"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 5, "end_line": 8, "quoted_text": "ISO-004,site_A,wound,2,1,0\nISO-005,site_B,urine,0.06,0,0\nISO-006,site_B,blood,16,1,1\nISO-007,site_B,sputum,0.125,0,1"}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "The report asserts the panel is used in the coding supplied and shows the correct supplied-coding agreement count of 17, which on its face suggests no complementation occurred; however, this is contradicted by the accompanying rate 0.291667 (= 7/24, not 17/24) and emission 11.2500 (= 7\u00d71 + 17\u00d70.25), both of which are only producible from the complemented comparison, and by the visible source code that complements the marker.", "observed_value": "claim of supplied coding plus count 17 alongside complement-based rate and emission", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 8, "end_line": 8, "quoted_text": "The reference panel is used in the coding in which it is supplied."}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 24, "end_line": 24, "quoted_text": "The reported agreement count is obtained by arithmetic from the count produced by the single per-unit equality comparison in the workflow; no second comparison is made."}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I tried to defeat my verdict two ways. First, I checked whether panel_indicator could be a legitimate recoding required by the data semantics; the task explicitly mandates using the panel values 'in the coding in which they are supplied,' and the data column panel_gyra_marker is already the reference call (1 = marker present), so complementing it has no stated justification and the report itself claims no recoding and no approved deviation. Second, I recomputed everything by hand from inputs/data.csv: supplied-coding matches = 17, misses = 7, so the supplied-coding emission would be 17\u00d71 + 7\u00d70.25 = 18.75 with rate 0.708333; the reported 11.25 and 0.291667 exactly equal the complement-based values (7 matches). Both checks confirm rather than falsify the issue.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}, {"case_id": "case:ba25407cb8c597e00a42", "verdict": "no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope", "bounded_statement": null, "root_cause": null, "issue_class": null, "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The workflow reads the panel column directly as supplied, with no complementation, and compares observed calls against it for the emission weights.", "observed_value": "panel_values taken verbatim from panel_gyra_marker", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 32, "end_line": 33, "quoted_text": "panel_values = [int(record[\"panel_gyra_marker\"]) for record in table_rows]\nweight_values = [concordance_weight(observed_calls[position], panel_values[position]) for position in range(unit_count)]"}, {"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 20, "end_line": 21, "quoted_text": "def concordance_weight(observed_value, panel_value):\n    return MISS_WEIGHT + (MATCH_WEIGHT - MISS_WEIGHT) * (observed_value == panel_value)"}]}, {"description": "The reported figures are internally consistent with the supplied-coding comparison: hand recount of inputs/data.csv gives 17 of 24 rows where observed_resistance_call equals panel_gyra_marker (discordant: ISO-004, ISO-007, ISO-011, ISO-015, ISO-018, ISO-021, ISO-023), so rate = 17/24 = 0.708333 and emission = 17\u00d71 + 7\u00d70.25 = 18.75, exactly as reported.", "observed_value": "17 of 24, rate 0.708333, emission 18.7500", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 16, "end_line": 18, "quoted_text": "Units whose observed call equals the supplied panel value: 17\nPer-unit agreement rate used by the emission accumulation: 0.708333\nAccumulated emission value (sum of the per-unit concordance weights): 18.7500"}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 20, "end_line": 20, "quoted_text": "[selected-result] Observed-versus-panel agreement is 17 of 24 units, per-unit agreement rate 0.708333, accumulated emission value 18.7500."}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "I looked for any complementation of the panel anywhere in the workflow source (a '1 - marker' transform, a second recoded panel list, or an inverted count such as unit_count minus a match count feeding the rate). None exists: agreement_count is taken directly as the numerator of the match count recovered from the emission total, and the rate uses that same count over the unit total, so there is no path by which a complemented panel could enter the reported figures.", "observed_value": "agreement_count and rate derived from the single direct comparison", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 46, "end_line": 47, "quoted_text": "agreement_count = matched_fraction.numerator\nagreement_rate = Fraction(agreement_count, unit_count)"}]}], "falsification_attempt": "To falsify a 'no issue' verdict I would need to find the complemented panel entering the emission or the reported rate. I traced every use of the panel column: it is read once as int(record[\"panel_gyra_marker\"]), used once in concordance_weight, and summed once for the descriptive panel_positive_total; no '1 - x' transform appears anywhere in the file. I then independently recomputed the expected supplied-coding results from the data (17 matches, rate 0.708333, emission 18.75) and confirmed the report states exactly these values; the complement-based alternative (rate 0.291667, emission 11.25) appears nowhere. The falsification attempt failed, supporting the no-issue verdict.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}, {"case_id": "case:be698ab19891acbd8e51", "verdict": "no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope", "bounded_statement": null, "root_cause": null, "issue_class": null, "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The emission weights are computed against panel_values taken directly from the supplied panel_allele column, not against the complement list.", "observed_value": "emission_weights use panel_values[index]", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 18, "end_line": 18, "quoted_text": "panel_values = [int(row[\"panel_allele\"]) for row in rows]"}, {"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 25, "end_line": 25, "quoted_text": "emission_weights = [agreement_weight(observed_values[index], panel_values[index], hit_weight, miss_weight) for index in range(total_units)]"}]}, {"description": "The reported figures match an independent recount against the supplied coding: 5 rows (rs1000103, rs1000106, rs1000111, rs1000116, rs1000121) have observed_call \u2260 panel_allele, so 19 matches, rate 19/24 = 0.791667, and product emission 1^19 \u00d7 (1/10)^5 = 1/100000, exactly as reported.", "observed_value": "19/24 = 0.791667, emission 1/100000", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 15, "end_line": 16, "quoted_text": "- sites whose observed call equals the staged panel allele: 19\n- per-unit agreement rate used by the emission accumulation: 19/24 = 0.791667"}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 28, "end_line": 28, "quoted_text": "[selected-result] panel-concordance emission for HG-PANEL-A over 24 assayed sites = 1/100000 = 0.000010000000 at agreement rate 19/24 = 0.791667"}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "The workflow does compute a complemented panel (complement_values = 1 - value) and a complement match count, which is the signature of the in-scope issue class; however, tracing its uses shows complement_flags feed only complement_match_count and the qc_total identity check, which the report explicitly labels as a quality-control comparison 'not used in the emission', and neither the emission product nor the agreement rate touches them.", "observed_value": "complement used only in a labeled QC check (5 sites; 19 + 5 = 24)", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 20, "end_line": 20, "quoted_text": "complement_values = [1 - value for value in panel_values]"}, {"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 24, "end_line": 24, "quoted_text": "complement_flags = [agreement_weight(observed_values[index], complement_values[index], 1, 0) for index in range(total_units)]"}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 19, "end_line": 22, "quoted_text": "## Quality-control comparison (not used in the emission)\n\n- sites whose observed call equals the strand-complemented panel value (1 - panel allele): 5\n- control check, concordant + complement-matching sites = total: 19 + 5 = 24"}]}], "falsification_attempt": "The presence of complement_values in the source is exactly what the issue class predicts, so I tried hard to show it reaches the selected result. Tracing dataflow: complement_values feeds only complement_flags; complement_flags feeds only complement_match_count; complement_match_count feeds only qc_total and the QC line of the report text. The emission product iterates over emission_weights, which are built from panel_values (the supplied coding), and agreement_rate is built from agreement_flags, also on panel_values. As a numeric cross-check, a complement-based emission would be 1^5 \u00d7 (1/10)^19 = 1e-19 with rate 5/24 = 0.208333; the report instead states 1/100000 and 19/24, matching the supplied-coding computation I verified row by row against inputs/data.csv. The falsification attempt failed; the complement appears only in a clearly labeled QC check excluded from the emission.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}]}